### 🟠 High Priority (9)

**9. EbookProjectsPanel.tsx — Silent Image Upload Failure**
`catch { /* silently ignore */ }` — user has zero feedback when cover/author image upload fails.

**10. EbookProjectsPanel.tsx — Race Condition on Image Upload**
Multiple uploads share `imageTargetRef.current`. Quickly clicking two upload buttons overwrites the ref; the wrong project gets the wrong image.

**11. route.ts — Inconsistent GET Response Shape**
Returns `{ books: [] }`, `{ manifest: ... }`, or `{ error: ... }` depending on branch. Client cannot reliably type this; leads to silent runtime errors.

**12. route.ts — Unvalidated LLM Enum Output**
`removedCategories: string[]` returned by the LLM is never validated against an enum. Unexpected strings break downstream switch logic.

**13. route.ts — Missing Section Structure Validation**
`chapter.sections.map(...)` is called after only a shallow `Array.isArray` check; if sections is `undefined`, the app crashes.

**14. ebook-quality.ts — Overlap Threshold Too Low**
A 3.5% n-gram overlap threshold means a 200-word section needs only ~7 words of sourced content to pass quality checks. Threshold should scale with word count (minimum ~15%).

**15. EbookProgressRing.tsx — SVG Text Centering Broken**
`style={{ transform: \`rotate(90deg) translate(0px, -${size}px)\` }}` on an SVG `<text>` element produces unpredictable cross-browser offset. Use `textAnchor="middle"` with explicit `x`/`y` attributes instead.

**16. page.tsx — `localStorage` Failure Silent**
Storage errors are caught and return `null`, indistinguishable from "no data". User loses pipeline state with no indication.

**17. route.ts — No Manifest Completeness Check**
`generatePdfBuffer(manifest, ...)` is called even when `manifest.chapters` is empty, producing a useless document.

